{
  "$comment": [
    "i18n key manifest for the LinkedIn-parity build.",
    "",
    "FOUR catalogs must stay in lockstep, and `pnpm check:i18n` enforces it:",
    "  apps/web/messages/ar-PS.json   apps/web/messages/en.json",
    "  apps/mobile/src/i18n/ar.json   apps/mobile/src/i18n/en.json",
    "",
    "Baseline before this build: web 979 keys / 32 namespaces, mobile 867 / 29.",
    "",
    "ARABIC IS AUTHORED FIRST. English is the fallback. A key that exists in en",
    "but not ar-PS is a defect, not a work-in-progress.",
    "",
    "Keys listed here are LEAF paths within their namespace. A key ending in",
    ".one/.other is an ICU plural and needs `zero`, `one`, `two`, `few`, `many`",
    "and `other` in Arabic — all six. Arabic plural rules are the single most",
    "common i18n defect in this codebase's category and next-intl will not warn.",
    "",
    "BEFORE adding any new namespace, run `pnpm check:i18n` and delete every key",
    "it flags as dead. Master spec §19.1 — new keys must not hide old rot."
  ],
